    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a122d0e_fe7ac822",
        "filename": "keystone_tempest_plugin/services/identity/base_clients.py",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 11022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-04-20T15:15:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we have the egg/chicken problem here, that\u0027s why I\u0027ve used the set_test_case() method.\n\nusually, tempest tests have a data generator which creates/destroy the fixtures for some default data, like users and projects. For tests that don\u0027t use generic data, they create/deletes the entities as required (so we would need to remember to use the self.addCleanup() every time).\n\nI\u0027m ok with removing the \"set_test_case()\" method and doing the cleanUp every time we create an entity.",
      "parentUuid": "1a122d0e_2d46dc4e",
      "revId": "61665dd27f595b43f0954064939c737e10965a78",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a122d0e_8be6e6e5",
